[AHA/ACC Guideline: High Cholesterol Management]
For patients with serum cholesterol exceeding 240 mg/dl and elevated blood pressure,lifestyle interventions include a low-sodium, heart-healthy diet,
regular aerobic exercise (150 mins/week),and consultation with a primary care physician for statin therapy evaluation.

[AHA/ACC Guideline: High Blood Pressure Triage]
Resting blood pressure exceeding 140/90 mm Hg is classified as Stage 2 Hypertension.
 Immediate lifestyle modifications, reduction of dietary sodium, and regular cardiovascular monitoring are strongly advised.

[AHA/ACC Guideline: Exercise-Induced Angina]
If exercise-induced angina or ST depression (oldpeak > 1.0) is present during physical exertion,
patients should avoid high-intensity isometric stress and undergo immediate diagnostic stress testing or a cardiology referral.